LANTERN — FOUR TRUE-HEADING SWEEP NATIVE TESTS

Four complete ready-to-ready tests: world+X/down-right, world+Z/down-left, world−X/up-left, world−Z/up-right. Each uses nine unique drawings. Repeated ready or recovery cels are not additional drawings. No hero mirroring.

OPEN
preview/sweep_four_directions_playable.html is a self-contained offline player with direction, replay, speed and scrub controls. Gameplay view uses the13m vertical span; close-up changes viewing size only. preview/sweep_four_directions_equal_worldsize.mp4 shows all four at matching approximate world size.

IMPORT
Each clips/<direction>/animation.json uses the same drawing/timeline schema. Sprite files, per-texture pixels_per_unit, image dimensions and pivots in both top-left pixels and normalized bottom-left coordinates are provided. Play the timed drawing IDs once and hold the final ready. Keep ready and action textures separate when their sampling densities differ. Do not apply one PPU to every texture indiscriminately.

The new+Z,−X,−Z action pixels were cropped and placed by integer translation only. Their one global sampling density is243,258 and220PPU respectively; shared ready uses nominal350PPU. Native action atlases are separate from ready. The earlier+X runtime uses350PPU with uniform whole-source registration from higher-resolution individual drawings; its original natives are included. Neither method uses anatomical deformation.

