QUALITY / LIMITS
Selected poses were reviewed first as ordinary, believable human movement. A failed detached-sword sheet and doubtful high-lantern cel are excluded. The +Z repeated horizontal recovery cel softens the large arm return; its chamber remains visually crowded at sword/lantern hand. The −X direct return is coarse but preferable to the rejected knee re-lift trial. −Z has a small final foot/hip settle. Minor native shape, footprint, costume and prop variation remains.

The up-left ready sword is fully hidden behind the coat along its projected far-side wrist-to-tip segment. Complete occlusion is physically defensible, though unseen pixels cannot prove a drawing. The +X test still uses its earlier approved ready source; it was not silently swapped for the later directional-ready sheet.

No combat hitboxes or event timings are included. Clip durations are provisional visual timings. The offline player logic was tested; a browser visual playback test was unavailable in the execution environment. MP4 decoding and ZIP integrity were checked.
